So a hit resets the streak. The streak only accumulates on null frames. If we make INTERACT_HOLD_FRAMES = 30, the prompt/target survives up to 30 consecutive null frames (0.5s at 60fps).

That's a reasonable, safe product-side robustness fix that aligns with the intent. It directly addresses the flake (a flicker at the cone edge clearing the target) and also improves real UX.

But — is increasing the hold the right fix, or a band-aid? The deeper issue: a target sitting right at the cone edge flickers in and out. Even with the hold, the prompt would visibly flicker (text appears/disappears… no, the hold prevents disappearance within 0.5s). With a 0.5s hold, a 10Hz flicker (100ms on / 100ms off) would never clear, because the off period (100ms = 6 frames) is less than 30 frames. The prompt stays up continuously.

So the 30-frame hold makes the prompt stable for targets at the cone edge. Good.

